akari369","id":1212726,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTI3MjY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1212726?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sakari369","html_url":"https://github.com/Sakari369","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sakari369/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sakari369/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sakari369/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sakari369/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sakari369/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sakari369/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sakari369/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sakari369/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sakari369/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-02-22T17:09:29Z","updated_at":"2019-02-22T17:09:29Z","body":"Thanks for the reply and info! I'm gonna leave this issue open for now, if somebody else comes across the same thing, not entirely trivial to connect this to vsync and mojave.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/glfw/glfw/issues/comments/466471515/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"Sakari369","id":1212726,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTI3MjY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1212726?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sakari369","html_url":"https://github.com/Sakari369","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sakari369/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sakari369/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sakari369/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sakari369/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sakari369/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sakari369/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sakari369/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sakari369/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sakari369/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/glfw/glfw/issues/comments/468022632","html_url":"https://github.com/glfw/glfw/issues/1435#issuecomment-468022632","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/glfw/glfw/issues/1435","id":468022632,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ2ODAyMjYzMg==","user":{"login":"AndrewBelt","id":338179,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzODE3OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/338179?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewBelt","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrewBelt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewBelt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewBelt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewBelt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewBelt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewBelt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewBelt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewBelt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewBelt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewBelt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-02-27T20:43:39Z","updated_at":"2019-02-28T05:21:53Z","body":"I'm not sure if @amarcu5's fix solves this entirely.\r\n\r\nI'm testing on a 2012 Macbook Pro Retina with Intel HD 4000 graphics. I wrote a simple loop\r\n```cpp\r\nwhile(!glfwWindowShouldClose(win)) {\r\n\tdouble startTime = glfwGetTime();\r\n\tglfwPollEvents();\r\n\tglfwSwapBuffers(win);\r\n\tdouble endTime = glfwGetTime();\r\n\tprintf(\"%g fps\\n\", 1 / (endTime - startTime));\r\n}\r\n\r\n```\r\nand out of a 30s profile, 16s were spent in the `[NSOpenGLContext flushBuffer]` method, which is directly called by `glfwSwapBuffers`, indicating that over 50% of a thread was used. This isn't the case on MacOS 10.13 or less, just 10.14 (Mojave).\r\n\r\n<img width=\"569\" alt=\"screen shot 2019-02-27 at 3 28 38 pm\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/338179/53521108-4c8f8600-3aa5-11e9-9281-7dcd4860545d.png\">\r\n\r\nUsing @amarcu5's fork consistently gives better results.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"552\" alt=\"screen shot 2019-02-27 at 3 31 09 pm\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/338179/53521110-4d281c80-3aa5-11e9-827f-d48c066f6621.png\">\r\n\r\nBut the expected result is that swapping buffers should only take 1-4% of CPU time per thread. Not sure what's going on with Apple's `flushBuffer` method.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/glfw/glfw/issues/comments/468022632/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"AndrewBelt","id":338179,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzODE3OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/338179?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewBelt","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrewBelt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewBelt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewBelt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewBelt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewBelt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewBelt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewBelt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewBelt/repos","ev